Golf With Your Friends is probably one of the top games you will get on the store for it's price. With the sale going on as we speak, I highly suggest picking up the game, even if it is to just have in your library. As the alpha testing currently shows, this game can prove to blow up to be huge one day.
//There is a very open and welcoming community to join into. I have been invited to play with about 5 different strangers in the course of 3 days of having the game just for being online.
//Balance between competitive and chill gameplay. You can choose when to tryhard and don't have to worry about slacking a few games.
//Achievements are definitely something to strive for as this game is still being developed.
//Costs very little compared to other titles.
//Mutator settings add variety to gameplay.
//Multiplayer is both fun and exciting in a public server or a private lobby of your own.
//Free roam in multiplayer lobby is definitely a new idea for a golf game.
//Already has huge player base.
//Other than poor RGB sliders, the game has little customization implementations.
//Offers little replayability. Does begin to get repetitive as you play the game.
//Visuals are on the low side (thus far)
I definitely do see this game going places in the future. I have seen how responsive the develpopers and moderators are both in discord and through steam. They do make sure to keep up with how the community is coming along, and how the growth of the game as well. Like I said, this game is still in it's alpha stages and has plenty of room for improvement to become outstanding so I will positively give this game a 92/100 in  it's early days. I look forward to seeing how well this game turns out!

