Those videos sure make the game look fun, so I purchased it a year ago. There were a lot of bugs initially but the game was officially "GREEN LIGHT" and in beta. There used to be fun Holiday events which helped you enjoy the game a lot more. Lets fast forward to today;
1-2 patches a day, no holiday events, and a lot of those same bugs which existed back in green light still exist today. I started playing the Island map in anticipation of the winter event and found that resources are not respawning on the map. Sea creatures I tamed randomly swim off and out of sight when I dismount them, creatures glitch through walls, fall from the sky, etc. Originally I would have recommended this game but I wouldn't recommend this to anyone now. Their "official" community support server is worse than their game failing to even let you register so you are left with Zero suppoirt.
I would say this to the Studio Wildcard team, you had a great game. Have you played it yourselves lately?
